      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Actually, let me reconsider attacking with Visionary. If I attack:\n\
- They can block with Brushstrider (3/1 vigilance). Visionary 3/3 kills Brushstrider, Brushstrider deals 3 to Visionary, Visionary survives at 3/3 with 3 damage... wait no, 3 damage kills a 3/3 since it has 3 toughness. Both die.\n\
- But I have Titanic Growth and Might of the Masses as combat tricks. If they block, I can use Titanic Growth to save my Visionary (+4/+4 makes it 7/7, survives).\n\
\n\
Hmm, but if they don't block, I deal 3 and save my trick. And I have mana for tricks (1 Forest + Visionary for Titanic Growth at {1}{G}).\n\
\n\
Wait - if I attack with Visionary, I can't tap Visionary for mana. So I'd only have 1 Forest for tricks. That's only enough for Might of the Masses ({G}).\n\
\n\
Let me just skip combat this turn. Archdruid is sick and Visionary is my only attacker. Better to wait until next turn when Archdruid can tap for mana during combat and I have more options.",
