      "player": "Opus Brewer",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Interesting - the Turntimber Basilisk's landfall triggered (they played Evolving Wilds → fetched a Forest), forcing Dwynen's Elite to block the Basilisk! So Elite is already assigned as a blocker for Basilisk.\n\
\n\
Brushstrider (3/1 vigilance) is attacking unblocked. I can block with the Elf Warrior Token (1/1) but it won't kill Brushstrider and the token dies. Actually wait - the token has Presence of Gond on it. I can't afford to lose it!\n\
\n\
If I don't block Brushstrider: I take 3 damage (11 → 8). But I keep my Gond token alive.\n\
If I block with Token: Token dies (only 1 toughness vs 3 power), Brushstrider survives. I lose Presence of Gond.\n\
\n\
The Basilisk has deathtouch and Elite is forced to block it. Elite dies to deathtouch, Basilisk takes 2 damage and dies (3/2 with 2 damage). Good trade actually.\n\
\n\
I absolutely cannot sacrifice my Gond token. Take the 3 damage.",
