      "ts": "2026-03-09T00:55:24.940153-07:00",
      "seq": 104,
      "player": "Opus Brewer",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Turn 6! I'm at 8 life. I drew Skyway Sniper (1/2 reach Elf for {G}). My Elf Warrior Token is no longer sick so I can activate Presence of Gond!\n\
\n\
Let me think about my plan:\n\
1. **Activate Presence of Gond** - tap the token to create another 1/1 Elf token\n\
2. **Cast Skyway Sniper** ({G}) - another Elf body, 1/2 with reach\n\
3. **Band Together** ({2}{G}) - I can use two of my creatures to kill Brushstrider\n\
\n\
Actually, let me think about Band Together. If I use Visionary (2/2) + any other creature to target Brushstrider (3/1), I deal 2+1=3 or 2+2=4 damage (depending on which creature). Brushstrider has 1 toughness, so even a single 1/1 token dealing damage would kill it. But Band Together says \"up to two target creatures you control each deal damage equal to their power to another target creature.\" So I just need any creature with power ≥1 to kill Brushstrider.\n\
\n\
Wait, let me re-read: \"Up to two target creatures you control each deal damage equal to their power to another target creature.\" So I pick up to 2 of my creatures and one enemy creature. Each of my creatures deals its power to the enemy. Just Visionary alone would deal 2, killing Brushstrider.\n\
\n\
Plan:\n\
1. Activate Presence of Gond (tap token → create 1/1 Elf)\n\
2. Cast Skyway Sniper ({G}) \n\
3. Cast Band Together ({2}{G}) targeting Visionary to deal 2 to Brushstrider\n\
\n\
Total mana: 4 Forests + Visionary = 5G. Skyway Sniper costs G, Band Together costs 2G. That's 3G total. Presence of Gond activation is free (just tap).\n\
\n\
Let me start by activating Presence of Gond:",
