      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "I have Might of the Masses available for {G}. With 8 creatures on my board (3 Elf tokens, Visionary, Skyway Sniper, Primeval Herald) plus Elven Bow and Presence of Gond as permanents... wait, Might of the Masses counts creatures I control. Let me count: 3 Elf tokens, Visionary, Skyway Sniper, Primeval Herald = 6 creatures. So it would give +6/+6 to one of my attackers.\n\
\n\
If I pump Skyway Sniper (1/2), it becomes 7/8, dealing 7 damage instead of 1. With the token's 1, that's 8 total. They go from 20 to 12.\n\
\n\
If I pump the Elf token (1/1), it becomes 7/7, dealing 7 damage instead of 1. Same total: 8 damage.\n\
\n\
I should pump for maximum damage! But should I save it? At 8 life, I need to be aggressive since they're building a board with Zendikar's Roil. Let's pump Skyway Sniper (less likely to die since it has reach and I want to keep it as a blocker... but it's tapped attacking).\n\
\n\
Actually, I should save Might of the Masses for a defensive situation or a lethal attack. 8 damage now brings them to 12, and I'd need to find another 12. If I hold it, I have it for defense or for a lethal alpha strike later. With Presence of Gond generating tokens every turn, my creature count will keep growing, making Might even better later.\n\
\n\
But they're about to have 2/2 tokens every turn from Zendikar's Roil. Pressure now might be better. Let me pump and deal 8.",
