      "reasoning": "Wait - they blocked! Both are sick though... Let me re-read. The Elemental Token blocks my 7/7 Elf, and Oashra Cultivator (0/3) blocks Skyway Sniper (1/2). \n\
\n\
Wait, they're sick! How are they blocking? Let me check...\n\
\n\
Actually, \"sick\" means summoning sickness - creatures can't attack with summoning sickness, but they CAN block. I forgot that rule!\n\
\n\
So my 7/7 Elf kills their 2/2 Elemental (and deals 5 trample? No, the Elf doesn't have trample). And my 1/2 Sniper trades into their 0/3 Cultivator - actually Sniper does 1 damage, Cultivator has 3 toughness, so Cultivator survives and deals 0 back. Sniper lives too since Cultivator has 0 power.\n\
\n\
No damage gets through to the player. That's unfortunate. At least I kill their Elemental token.",
