      "reasoning": "I could equip Elven Bow to one of my tokens for defense. It costs {1} to equip and gives +1/+2. That would make a 1/1 into a 2/3, which could help block.\n\
\n\
Actually, I should equip it to my 5/5 Elf token (which goes back to 1/1 end of turn when Titanic Growth wears off). Wait, no - Titanic Growth lasts until end of turn, so it's still 5/5. But it's tapped so I can't equip it this turn anyway... actually equipping doesn't require the creature to be untapped.\n\
\n\
Let me equip the Elven Bow to the sick Elf token (p130) - it'll make it a 2/3 which can block better. Or actually, I should equip it to one that can block. The sick one can block! All creatures can block regardless of summoning sickness.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me think about what's coming. Next turn they attack with Baloths (6/6 trample), Beast (4/4), Elemental (2/2), and possibly Cultivator (0/3). That's 12 damage and I'm at 8. I need to block at least 4 damage.\n\
\n\
I have 4 Elf tokens (3 will be untapped next turn - the sick one won't untap but CAN block). So I can block with all 4 tokens.\n\
\n\
Equipping Elven Bow to one token makes it 2/3. If I block the 4/4 Beast with the 2/3 token, it dies but trades better. If I block the 6/6 Baloths with a 1/1, it takes 1 off (but trample means 5 still comes through).\n\
\n\
I need to survive. Equip the bow for better blocking:",
